<h2 class="bde-heading-506-128 bde-heading">
Why Is Paul Reed on $5.6m in 2026-27?
</h2><div class="bde-fancy-container-506-129 bde-fancy-container">
  
  
	



<div class="bde-fancy-container-506-145 bde-fancy-container">
  
  
	



<div class="bde-f-text-506-158 bde-f-text">
<p>Reed is paid <strong>$5.6m</strong> because a center who rebounds and defends is useful at almost any price, and a 58th pick never gets to argue about what that price is.</p>
<ul>
<li>He went 58th in 2020 and his first three seasons paid him <strong>$3.91m</strong> in total.</li>
<li>Philadelphia gave him <strong>$23.56m</strong> over three years in 2023 with only <strong>$7.72m</strong> of it guaranteed.</li>
<li>Two seasons of that contract were tied to Philadelphia winning a playoff round.</li>
<li>He was waived inside it and claimed by Detroit, which is why 2024-25 has no published figure.</li>
<li>This season started out unprotected until January 10, 2027.</li>
</ul>
<p>Almost every contract he has signed has had a guarantee date attached to it.</p>

